        '0.14': '"Or perhaps she is kept hidden in Ravana\'s house, and the young lady wails bitterly like a mynah in a cage."',
        '0.15': '"Born in Janaka\'s family, Rama\'s wife, slender-waisted and lotus-eyed — how could she ever come under Ravana\'s power?"',
        '0.16': '"Whether Janaka\'s daughter is lost, vanished or dead, it is not fit to report it to Rama, who loves his wife so dearly."',
        '0.17': '"There is harm in telling and harm in not telling; how indeed should I act? It seems a hard dilemma to me."',
        '0.18': '"In this situation, what would be timely and right?" So Hanuman pondered again and again.',
        '0.19': '"If I go from here to the monkey king\'s city without seeing Sita, what will my manly effort be worth?"',
        '0.20': '"My leap across the ocean will have been in vain, and my entry into Lanka and my seeing of the rakshasas too."',
        '0.21': '"What will Sugriva say, or the assembled monkeys, or those two sons of Dasaratha, when I reach Kishkindha?"',
        '0.22': '"If I go and tell Kakutstha the harsh words, \'I have not seen Sita,\' then he will give up his life."',
        '0.23': '"Hearing such harsh, cruel, piercing, heart-searing ill news about Sita, he will not survive."',
        '0.24': '"Seeing him in such distress, his mind set on death, the wise Lakshmana, so deeply devoted to him, will not survive either."',
        '0.25': '"Hearing that both brothers have perished, Bharata too will die; and seeing Bharata dead, Shatrughna will not live."',
        '0.26': '"Seeing their sons dead, the mothers — Kausalya, Sumitra and Kaikeyi — will not survive; of that there is no doubt."',
        '0.27': '"Grateful and true to his word, Sugriva, lord of the monkeys, seeing Rama in that state, will then give up his life."',
        '0.28': '"Heartbroken, pained, wretched and joyless, afflicted by grief for her husband, poor Ruma will give up her life."',
        '0.29': '"Queen Tara too, already tormented by grief for Vali and worn thin by sorrow, will die and not survive."',
        '0.30': '"Through the loss of his mother and father and Sugriva\'s calamity, Prince Angada too will give up his life."',
        '0.31': '"Overwhelmed by grief for their master, the forest-dwellers will beat their heads with their palms and fists."',
        '0.32': '"Cherished by the famous monkey king with kind words, gifts and honour, the monkeys will give up their lives."',
        '0.33': '"No more will the great monkeys gather to play in the forests, on the mountains or in secluded retreats."',
        '0.34': '"With their sons, wives and ministers, stricken by their master\'s calamity, they will hurl themselves from mountain peaks onto level and rugged ground."',
        '0.35': '"The monkeys will resort to poison, hanging, entering fire, fasting, or the sword."',
        '0.36': '"I think a terrible wailing will arise when I go back — the ruin of the Ikshvaku race and of the forest-dwellers as well."',
        '0.37': '"So I shall not go from here to the city of Kishkindha; I cannot bear to face Sugriva without Maithili."',
        '0.38': '"If I do not go but stay here, those two righteous great warriors will live on in hope, and so will the swift monkeys."',
        '0.39': '"Without having seen Janaka\'s daughter, I shall become a forest hermit, living at the foot of trees, self-restrained, eating only what falls into my hand or mouth."',
        '0.40': '"On the seashore, in a place rich in roots, fruits and water, I will build a pyre and enter the blazing fire kindled from the fire-sticks."',
        '0.41': '"Or, as I sit fasting unto death in due form, crows and beasts of prey will eat my body."',
        '0.42': '"This too is a way of departure approved by the sages, I believe: I shall duly enter the waters if I do not see Janaki."',
        '0.43': '"My lovely, well-rooted and glorious garland of fame is shattered for ever, since I have not found Sita."',
        '0.44': '"Or I shall become an ascetic, self-restrained, living at the foot of trees; I will not go back from here without seeing the dark-eyed lady."',
        '0.45': '"If I go back without finding Sita, Angada and all the monkeys with him will not survive."',
        '0.46': '"Yet death brings many evils, while one who lives may gain good fortune. So I shall hold on to life; for the living, reunion is certain."',
        '0.47': 'Bearing in his mind such manifold sorrow, the elephant among monkeys could not then reach the far shore of his grief.',
        '0.48': 'Then the steadfast great monkey summoned his valour: "Or I will kill the mighty ten-headed Ravana; even if Sita has been carried off, she will be avenged."',
        '0.49': '"Or I will lift him up, carry him high over the ocean and present him to Rama, like a victim offered to Pashupati."',
        '0.50': 'Thus sunk in anxiety at not finding Sita, his mind filled with brooding and grief, the monkey reflected:',
