        '0.26': 'he reasoned, on grounds that supported it, that this was Sita — as she had been seen then, being carried off by that shape-shifting rakshasa.',
        '0.27': '"For this lady has just the form in which she was seen then." Her face like the full moon, fine-browed, with lovely rounded breasts,',
        '0.28': 'the queen lit up all the quarters with her radiance, dispelling darkness; dark-throated, with lips like bimba fruit, slender-waisted, well-formed,',
        '0.29': 'Sita, with eyes like lotus petals, like Rati, the beloved of Manmatha, dear to the whole world, like the radiance of the full moon;',
        '0.30': 'the fair-bodied one sat on the ground like an ascetic woman under vows, timid, sighing deeply, like the wife of a serpent king;',
        '0.31': 'not shining, because of the great net of grief spread over her, like a flame of fire clinging to a veil of smoke.',
        '0.32': 'She was like a memory clouded with doubt, like prosperity fallen, like faith shattered, like hope frustrated,',
